 			<p>Amy followed, but she poked her hands out stiffly before her, and jerked herself along as if she went by machinery; and her “Ow!” was more suggestive of pins being run into her than of fear and anguish. Jo gave a despairing groan, and Meg laughed outright, while Beth let her bread burn as she watched the fun, with interest.</p>
 			<p>“It’s no use! Do the best you can when the time comes, and if the audience laugh, don’t blame me. Come on, Meg.”</p>
